[Ranking sites and betting sites are websites dedicated to rating and ranking parahumans, both heroes and villains. These sites track the wins and losses of capes, with rankings based on factors such as a cape's presence in the news and their success in fights. Capes who lay low or are overshadowed by larger news stories may see their ratings drop.

Ranking sites offer various incentives for capes, such as income from hosting live streams, participating in online interviews, or offering prizes. Some sites even sponsor parahumans, similar to a corporate team but with fewer conditions, primarily focusing on the cape's ability to maintain their ratings. Villains like Bambina can receive money from sponsors based on their ranking, with the amount fluctuating based on their performance.

Notable users of ranking and betting sites include Bambina, Meathead, and Ova.]

[If a Cape views a Ranking Site, generate the following website, Cape Watch, in the next response using the provided format:

<div class="ranking-site">
  <h1>Cape Watch</h1>
  <div class="cape-list">
    <div class="cape-item">
      <h2>Cape Name 1</h2>
      <p>Rank: <span class="rank">1</span></p>
      <p>Wins: <span class="wins">25</span></p>
      <p>Losses: <span class="losses">5</span></p>
    </div>
    <div class="cape-item">
      <h2>Cape Name 2</h2>
      <p>Rank: <span class="rank">2</span></p>
      <p>Wins: <span class="wins">20</span></p>
      <p>Losses: <span class="losses">8</span></p>
    </div>
    <!-- Add more cape items for the top 4 capes -->
    <div class="cape-item">
      <h2>Skitter/Weaver</h2>
      <p>Rank: <span class="rank">5</span></p>
      <p>Wins: <span class="wins">18</span></p>
      <p>Losses: <span class="losses">7</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

2. Apply the following CSS styles to enhance the visual appearance:

<style>
  .ranking-site {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .cape-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    grid-gap: 20px;
  }

  .cape-item {
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    padding: 10px;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>

3. Dynamically update the rankings, wins, and losses based on the latest data and context of the story. Ensure that Taylor, as Skitter or Weaver (depending on the story's progress), is always included as the 5th cape, regardless of her current ranking.]

[Betting sites, such as "Shard Gamble," allow users to wager on the outcomes of cape battles. These sites showcase upcoming battles between capes, providing information such as the date, location, and betting odds for each matchup. Users can place bets on their preferred outcomes, adding an element of excitement and speculation to the cape scene.

Betting sites operate by collecting wagers from users and distributing the winnings based on the actual outcome of the battles. They make money by taking a percentage of the total bets as a commission. Some betting sites also offer live streaming of the battles, allowing users to watch the events unfold in real-time while placing their bets.

The odds on these sites are determined by various factors, including the capes' rankings, their previous performance, and public perception. As battles occur and capes' reputations change, the odds are dynamically updated to reflect the current state of the cape scene.]

If a Cape views a betting website, generate the following content in the next response, following the provided format:

1. Use the provided HTML template to structure the betting site:

<div class="betting-site">
  <h1>Shard Gamble</h1>
  <div class="betting-list">
    <div class="betting-item">
      <h2>Upcoming Battle: [Cape 1] vs. [Cape 2]</h2>
      <p>Date: <span class="date">[Date]</span></p>
      <p>Location: <span class="location">[Location]</span></p>
      <div class="betting-odds">
        <p>[Cape 1]: <span class="odds">[Odds 1]</span></p>
        <p>[Cape 2]: <span class="odds">[Odds 2]</span></p>
      </div>
      <button class="place-bet">Place Bet</button>
    </div>
    <!-- Add more betting items for upcoming battles -->
  </div>
</div>

2. Apply the provided CSS styles to enhance the visual presentation:

<style>
  .betting-site {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .betting-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    grid-gap: 20px;
  }

  .betting-item {
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    padding: 10px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .betting-odds {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-around;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .place-bet {
    padding: 5px 10px;
    background-color: #007bff;
    color: #fff;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
</style>

3. Dynamically generate the upcoming battles, dates, locations, and betting odds based on the current state of the story and the Cape viewing the website. Include at least 3 upcoming battles, with one of them involving the Cape viewing the site (if applicable).

4. Ensure that the betting odds reflect the realistic chances of each Cape winning based on their abilities, reputation, and recent performance.]

[Parahumans Online (PHO) is the premier website for cape-related news, gossip, and information. It features message boards, a wiki, chatrooms, and private messaging functionality. The site plays a crucial role in establishing and popularizing cape names, with the community often simplifying or changing names to meet certain standards.

PHO's message boards are the most prominent feature, with various people, such as Taylor, Lisa, and Greg, using the platform to discuss cape activities. The wiki provides information on cape groups and events, as well as warnings about dangerous parahumans like Hellhound and Oni Lee.

The site's cultural impact is significant, as carelessly chosen or offensive names can be misinterpreted or renamed by the community. When a villain dies, their name becomes available, but taking it without consideration can lead to inherited bad reputations and rivalries. Heroes, on the other hand, are more likely to ask for permission to use a name.

PHO serves as a central hub for the parahuman community, facilitating communication, information sharing, and the shaping of cape identities. Its influence cannot be overstated, as it acts as a primary source of information and interaction for both capes and civilians alike.

If someone views the Parahumans Online website, generate the following content:

1. Use the provided HTML template to structure the website:

<div class="pho-website">
  <header>
    <h1>Parahumans Online</h1>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section id="news">
      <h2>Latest Cape-Related News</h2>
      <!-- Add news articles based on the current context -->
    </section>

    <section id="message-boards">
      <h2>Message Boards</h2>
      <!-- Add message board threads and posts -->
    </section>

    <section id="chatroom">
      <h2>Public Chatroom</h2>
      <!-- Add chatroom messages and input field -->
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2023 Parahumans Online. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>
</div>

2. Apply the following CSS styles to enhance the visual presentation:

<style>
  .pho-website {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  footer {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 20px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #ccc;
  }
</style>

3. Dynamically generate the content for each section based on the current context of the story:

   - In the "Latest Cape-Related News" section, include relevant news articles, headlines, and snippets that reflect the current events and developments in the story.
   - In the "Message Boards" section, display message board threads and posts that discuss topics related to the current situation, such as cape activities, rumors, and theories.
   - In the "Public Chatroom" section, show ongoing conversations between various PHO users, including speculations, reactions, and discussions about the current events.

4. Ensure that the generated content is consistent with the established tone, style, and formatting of the Parahumans Online website, and that it accurately reflects the current state of the story and the user's perspective.]
